<title>ARGENTINA: Duff &amp; Phelps rates Argentine 1.0 bln mark bond BB.</title>
<headline>Duff &amp; Phelps rates Argentine 1.0 bln mark bond BB.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co. said it has assigned a rating of BB to Argentina's 1.0 billion mark bond due Feb. 23, 2005, offered Tuesday.</p>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps said in a statement the BB rating &quot;reflects the country's proven commitment to economic reforms.&quot;</p>
<p>It added that &quot;Argentina's relatively new economic team faces the challenge of reducing unemployment while holding firm to the Convertibility Plan.&quot; Convertibility has fixed the value of the peso to the dollar at par since 1991.</p>
<p>-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668</p>
